>> title: Chawanmushi
>> category: Custards & Puddings
>> tags: egg custard, dashi, savoury, steamed, japanese
>> servings: 4
>> time: 40 min
>> step.1: warm, then cool to lukewarm
>> step.2: beat gently
>> step.3: stir in, then strain twice
>> step.5: steam 15 min
>> step.6: top with mitsuba

Warm @dashi{1 3/4%cup}(420 mL), @soy sauce{2%tsp}(10 mL), @mirin{2%tsp}(10 mL), @table salt{1/4%tsp} until the salt dissolves, then let it cool to lukewarm.

Beat @eggs{3%large}(150 g) gently, without working in any foam.

Stir @&(~2)seasoned dashi{} into @&(~1)eggs{}, then strain it twice.

Divide @shrimp{4%whole}(peeled), @boneless chicken thigh{2%oz}(60 g, in 1/2-in pieces), @shiitake mushrooms{2%whole}(thinly sliced), @kamaboko{4%slices}(fish cake) among #4 teacups{}.

Pour @&(~2)custard{} over @&(~1)garnishes{}, cover the cups, and steam in a #steamer{} over low heat for ~{15%min}.

Top @&(~1)chawanmushi{} with @mitsuba{4%sprigs}(or thinly sliced scallion).
